# TAK-PluginSuite-FeatureLink — root .gitignore covering all seven components
# (ATAK5.6, ATAK5.7 — Android/Gradle; WinTAK5.6, WinTAK5.7 — Visual Studio/.NET/WPF;
#  CloudTAK, TAKPortal — Node/TypeScript; Infra-TAK — Python/Flask)
#
# Rules here are ANCHORED wherever an unanchored pattern would over-match. The repository
# tracks 14,900 icon PNGs under paths that include directory names like `release`, so a bare
# `[Rr]elease/` is a live footgun rather than a theoretical one (audit Appendix E §2.4).

# ── Gradle / Android (ATAK5.6, ATAK5.7) ─────────────────────────────────────
.gradle/
**/build/
# (`**/build/` above already subsumes the former `**/app/build/` line — removed as redundant.)
gradle.properties
local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
*.dex
*.class
out/
gen/
captures/
proguard/

# Build-tool-generated cache file. `api.hash` is a real input and IS tracked, but the
# leading timestamp comment is rewritten on every build, so these two files show as
# modified with a comment-only diff and pad every review (audit Appendix E §4.2).
# NOTE: both files are already tracked, and an ignore rule does not affect a tracked file.
# Closing this fully needs `git rm --cached ATAK5.{6,7}/.takdev/plugin.properties` plus a
# committed, non-generated record of the two api.hash values — that touches the ATAK trees
# and is filed as a cross-package request in docs/remediation/wp5-crosscutting.md.
**/.takdev/plugin.properties

# ── Signing keys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.jks
*.keystore

# ── Visual Studio / .NET / WPF (WinTAK5.6, WinTAK5.7) ───────────────────────
.vs/
# Anchored: a bare `bin/`/`obj/` matches a Python `bin/` or any icon subdirectory at any
# depth. These are the only .NET build roots in the repository.
WinTAK5.6/bin/
WinTAK5.6/obj/
WinTAK5.7/bin/
WinTAK5.7/obj/
# Anchored for the same reason — `[Dd]ebug/`/`[Rr]elease/` unanchored matched any directory
# named debug/release at any depth, including under an icon corpus.
WinTAK5.6/bin/[Dd]ebug/
WinTAK5.6/bin/[Rr]elease/
WinTAK5.7/bin/[Dd]ebug/
WinTAK5.7/bin/[Rr]elease/
WinTAK5.6/[Dd]ebug/
WinTAK5.6/[Rr]elease/
WinTAK5.7/[Dd]ebug/
WinTAK5.7/[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.obj
packages/
*.nupkg
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt

# ── Node / TypeScript (CloudTAK, TAKPortal) ─────────────────────────────────
# The root file previously had NO node_modules rule at all — only CloudTAK/.gitignore did.
# An `npm install` inside TAKPortal/ would have staged thousands of files (Appendix E §2.1).
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Lockfiles are deliberately NOT ignored. `package-lock.json` is what makes `npm ci`
# reproducible and is the input to the CycloneDX SBOM generated in CI (C-30).

# ── Python (Infra-TAK) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── IDE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# ── Logs / profiling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.hprof

# ── OS junk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# (`**/.DS_Store` subsumes the former bare `.DS_Store` line — removed as redundant.)
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Backup files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Was the exact literal `README.md.bak`, which did not match `README2.md.bak` (13,173 b) —
# leaving a stale duplicate of the project's front page one `git add -A` from being
# committed. Both .bak files have since been deleted (Appendix E §2.4, §3.6).
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~

# ── Release artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Was a blanket `*.zip`, which correctly kept the nine release zips out of the index but
# would also silently swallow any legitimately-needed archive — a generated iconset
# fixture, a test-data package, a `.wpk`-adjacent bundle — with no negation anywhere.
# Scoped to the two places build output actually lands (Appendix E §2.4).
/*.zip
**/build/**/*.zip
**/dist/**/*.zip
*.wpk

# ── Environment / secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.json

# ── Keep these SDK support files — required by the ATAK builds ─────────────
!ATAK5.6/.takdev/
!ATAK5.6/.takdev/aars/
!ATAK5.6/.takdev/aars/*.aar
!ATAK5.6/buildtools/
!ATAK5.6/buildtools/atak-gradle-takdev.jar
!ATAK5.7/.takdev/
!ATAK5.7/.takdev/aars/
!ATAK5.7/.takdev/aars/*.aar
!ATAK5.7/buildtools/
!ATAK5.7/buildtools/atak-gradle-takdev.jar

# DEPRECATED NEGATIONS — scheduled for removal under C-40.
# These re-add the committed signing keystores. Appendix F §2.1 adjudicates C-40 as MEDIUM
# (the blob is the stock ATAK SDK dev key `wintec_mapping` / O=WinTec Arrowmaker, md5
# de161723bca27d5da9dd16052ee18cae, identical to the SDK's own android_keystore — it is
# already public worldwide, so there is no confidentiality loss and NO history rewrite is
# warranted). The negations are retained for now ONLY because removing an ignore rule does
# not untrack an already-tracked file: the real fix is `git rm --cached` on both blobs plus
# env-var-sourced signing passwords in ATAK5.{6,7}/app/build.gradle, which lives in another
# work package's tree. Removing these lines before that lands would change nothing except
# to make re-adding the file require `-f`. Tracked as a cross-package request.
!ATAK5.6/app/featurelink.keystore
!ATAK5.7/app/featurelink.keystore

# gradle.properties is ignored everywhere above (may carry machine-specific paths/secrets
# elsewhere), except these two — they only set a JVM heap size for R8, needed on any CI
# runner (GitHub Actions, TAK Product Center's submission pipeline) since a release build's
# R8 minification pass has hit OutOfMemoryError on the default heap.
!ATAK5.6/gradle.properties
# `!ATAK5.7/gradle.properties` was MISSING. ATAK5.7/gradle.properties was tracked only
# because it was already added (ignore rules do not affect tracked files) and because
# ATAK5.7/.gitignore's own `!gradle.properties` happened to win by specificity. If it were
# ever `git rm --cached`'d it could not be re-added without `-f` (Appendix E §2.4).
!ATAK5.7/gradle.properties

# Internal pre-award audit deliverable (capability/defect/test checklist).
# Local working artifact only - not part of the shipped suite, and it enumerates
# unremediated security findings, so it must never reach a remote.
FEATURELINK-AUDIT-CHECKLIST.md
